                <pb facs="0415" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8741½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Press Release Issued by the Department of State on
                        July 12, 1937</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1937-07-12">July 12, 1937</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>The Japanese Ambassador and the Counselor of the Chinese Embassy each called at
                    the Department this morning, and communicated information in regard to events in
                    North China. In the course of the conversations which ensued both were given
                    expression of the view that an armed conflict between Japan and China would be a
                    great blow to the cause of peace and world progress.</p>
            </div>
